==============================================================================
B2c. The SAME fault on the OTHER workload -- who sees it now?
==============================================================================

  prefill regression (+40%), prefill-heavy workload (4000-token prompt):
    ml.prefill_p50          800.01 ->   1120.01 ms    +40.0%
    ml.ttft_p50             802.52 ->   1122.52 ms    +39.9%
    sre.call_dur_p50       1025.45 ->   1346.51 ms    +31.3%
    ask.ttfm_p50            826.28 ->   1146.45 ms    +38.7%
    pm.e2e_p50             1025.45 ->   1346.51 ms    +31.3%

  Same fault, same code, same 40%. On decode-heavy it was 5 ms and only
  the ML engineer's dashboard moved (because their denominator is 13 ms).
  On prefill-heavy every dashboard moves. WHO SEES A FAULT IS A PROPERTY
  OF THE WORKLOAD MIX, not of the instrumentation -- which is why a
  percentage-based SLO means something different to each persona.

